# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore — REPOSITORY ROOT, not deployments/ ([OPS-06]).
# The build context is the repo root, so this file decides what the daemon
# uploads and what `COPY . .` can put into a layer.
#
# Two reasons it is not optional:
#   1. node_modules and deployments/map data are gigabytes. Sending them makes
#      every build slow even when nothing changed.
#   2. `COPY . .` without it puts .env.prod and .git into an image layer.
#      Deleting the file in a later RUN does not remove it from the layer;
#      anyone with the image can `docker save` and read it ([OPS-17]).
# =============================================================================

# Reinstalled by `npm ci` inside the image; a host copy is also the wrong
# platform (native bindings built for Windows/macOS).
node_modules
*/node_modules

# Built inside the image.
dist
build
.vite
coverage
playwright-report
test-results

# SECRETS. .env.example is the only env file allowed in the context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deployments/**/.env
deployments/**/.env.*
!deployments/**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12

# History and CI metadata are not build inputs. .git alone is often 200 MB+.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml

# Tile data, mbtiles archives and service volumes under deployments/ are for
# the map compose project, not for the frontend image. On the reference
# deployment this directory alone was 40 GB.
deployments/map
deployments/**/data
**/*.mbtiles
**/*.pmtiles

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Docs and agent instruction files do not affect the bundle.
docs
*.md
!README.md
